        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the Marie Rose sauce"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix {{mayonnaise}} of mayonnaise with {{ketchup}} of ketchup, {{worcestershire-sauce}} of Worcestershire sauce, and {{lemon-juice}} of lemon juice in a bowl. Add a pinch of cayenne if using. Stir until smooth. Taste: the sauce should be tangy, slightly sweet, and a pale salmon colour."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the {{prawns-cooked}} of cooked prawns to the sauce and toss to coat. Chill for at least 30 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assemble and serve"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Divide the shredded iceberg between four glasses or small bowls. Spoon the dressed prawns over the top."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Dust lightly with paprika, place a lemon wedge on the side, and serve at once."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "rows": [
            {
              "symptom": "Prawns are watery and dilute the sauce",
              "cause": "Pre-cooked frozen prawns not dried properly before dressing",
              "fix": "Tip the cooked prawns into a colander and leave to drain for 5 minutes, then pat dry with kitchen paper before mixing with the sauce."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Sauce is too sweet",
              "cause": "Too much ketchup or a sweet brand of ketchup",
              "fix": "Balance with more lemon juice or a few drops of Worcestershire sauce."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Lettuce is limp by the time it reaches the table",
              "cause": "Assembled too far in advance",
              "fix": "Shred the lettuce no more than 30 minutes before serving and keep it in the fridge until needed."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The prawn cocktail was the default British dinner-party starter from the 1960s through the early 1980s, served in a glass with a waved prawn balanced on the rim. It went out of fashion badly, became a shorthand for naff cooking, and then came back in the 2000s under the banner of retro revival. At a good pub or bistro it is now served without irony. The dish itself has not changed much: good prawns, a properly made sauce, and crisp lettuce is all it needs."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
